=============================================================================
 ASDD — Mixed (FE + BE) AGENTS.md template
=============================================================================
 This template is the third profile-specific starting point for the
 consumer's `AGENTS.md`, alongside `AGENTS.md.fe.example` and
 `AGENTS.md.be.example`. Use it when the same repo hosts BOTH frontend and
 backend code, in either of these shapes:

   1. Monorepo with physically separated FE and BE packages
      (e.g. `apps/web` + `apps/api`, `packages/ui` + `packages/server`).
   2. Monolith with FE and BE intermingled in the same package
      (e.g. ASP.NET MVC + Razor + JS, Next.js app + API routes,
      Django + templates, Rails, Laravel, Blazor).

 It is derived from and kept in sync with the canonical base at
 `asdd/ai-workflow/AGENTS.md`, which defines the 9-section canonical
 structure, the shared rules every ASDD-compatible AGENTS.md must enforce,
 and the required ASDD frontmatter.

 SSOT rule: this template does NOT duplicate the concrete FE / BE
 conventions from `AGENTS.md.fe.example` / `AGENTS.md.be.example`. Instead
 it splits `## Code Conventions` into `### Frontend` and `### Backend`
 subsections and points the reader at the two sibling templates for the
 rich starting content. Copy the pieces that apply from each into the
 matching subsection here.

 Sections marked with `<PLACEHOLDER>` MUST be filled in.
 Sections with concrete examples (paths, package names, versions) SHOULD be
 adapted to your repo — keep the same structure and level of detail.
=============================================================================
